# global-typescript-style

> **Purpose:** Make all code look and behave the same across the monorepo.
>
> **Applies to:** Every file in the repo (always on).

## TypeScript
- Use strict TypeScript and ESM everywhere.
- Never use `any`. Use `unknown` and parse it with Zod.
- Prefer `type` aliases for data shapes; derive shared shapes with `z.infer`.
- Mark function return types on every exported function.

## Naming
- Files: kebab-case (`hash-url.ts`). React components: PascalCase (`StepCard.tsx`). Hooks: `useX.ts`.
- Variables and functions: camelCase. Constants: UPPER_SNAKE_CASE.
- Booleans start with `is`, `has` or `should`.
- Slugs are lowercase app names (`hubspot`).

## Terms
- Say "provider OAuth app" and "user connection". Do not mix in synonyms.
- Use the label words exactly: Tested, Sourced, Uncertain.

## Lint and format
- ESLint (`@stamp/eslint-config`) and Prettier (root `.prettierrc`) must pass.
- Never disable a lint rule without a comment that says why.

## Errors
- Never swallow an error. Handle it, or rethrow it with a typed code.
- Never use `console.log` for real logging; use the logger.

## Commits
- Use conventional commits: `feat:`, `fix:`, `docs:`, `refactor:`, `test:`, `chore:`.
- One logical change per commit.
